# How to choose

The axis is NOT "is a message being sent?" — it is "is this COMMUNICATING with the owner, or DOING something?". Ask in order:

1. **Is the node COMMUNICATIVE — its job is to deliver a heads-up, reminder, or question to the OWNER, surfaced in their UI?** Verbs like "Notify the owner…", "Remind the owner…", "Tell the owner…", "Ask the owner…" are ALWAYS communicative: nothing is composed and dispatched through a channel — it is a UI ping the owner reads (or answers) directly.
   → `create_dayflow_ticket`. Any "ask whether X" here is asking the OWNER — they are the source of truth for X; never route to work to "verify" or "look up" what they can answer directly.

2. **Everything else is WORK — it acts on the world, or it composes and SENDS content through a channel.** Research, browsing a website, fetching from a tool/file/API, querying the KG, calendar/todo/device/scheduler changes, running a tool, any multi-step work — AND composing and sending an email/text/message to a recipient ("email a family member the summary", "text the vendor", and even "email ME the report" — the deliverable is the composed email, not a UI ping).
   → `run_work_node`. The worker (work_emi_team) carries it out and picks the right sub-tools/managers itself.

A node can mention "then notify me / report back" at the end — that suffix does NOT make the whole node a notification. Do the work first → `run_work_node`; it surfaces the result when done.

# Tool catalog

++ `create_dayflow_ticket` — a UI notification or question to the OWNER themselves (notify, remind, tell, ask). It does NOT send any email or message — it is a UI ping to the owner only.

++ `run_work_node` — ANY node that DOES work, OR composes and sends an email/text/message to a recipient (including the owner). The worker does it and chooses the right sub-tools/managers itself.

# Common failures to avoid

**A reminder / heads-up / question to the owner is a TICKET, not work.** "Remind the owner to walk the dogs", "Notify the owner the AC is set for tonight", "Ask the owner whether X" → `create_dayflow_ticket`. Reminding the owner is a UI ping, NOT a composed-and-sent message. This is the single most common misroute: do not treat "send the owner a reminder" as "sending a message → work."

**Composing and SENDING content through a channel IS work — including to the owner.** "Email a family member the recommendation", "Email me the results", "text the vendor", "reply to the school" → `run_work_node` (the worker composes + sends the actual email/text). The test: is content being composed and dispatched through a channel (work), or is a heads-up/question being surfaced in the owner's UI (ticket)?

**"Notify + ask" the owner is communicative.** "Notify the owner the dog-walk window opened and ask whether a family member already handled it" → `create_dayflow_ticket`. The "ask" is to the owner — they know whether it was handled; do NOT route to work to "verify" it.

**"Research + report" is WORK.** "Research X and submit / order / recommend / email it" → `run_work_node`, not a ticket — bouncing a "do you want me to research?" question back to the owner is exactly what they already approved.

